# Cloudflare Pages redirects — pretty Spanish vanity paths -> the real /es/* pages.
# Keeps declareandbelieve.com/bienvenido (shown in Ayuda y soporte) working while
# the canonical pages stay under /es/.
/bienvenido /es/bienvenido 301
/ayuda /es/ayuda 301
/luchas /es/luchas 301
/dar /pricing?lang=es 301
/acerca /es/acerca 301
/privacidad /es/privacidad 301
/terminos /es/terminos 301

# ── Live giving retired (hotfix) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The donation product is gone. The Worker already returns 410 for every
# /give/* payment endpoint, so these pages were inert; this removes them from
# view. One hop each, no chains.
#
# Cloudflare Pages does not match query strings, so the old success/cancelled
# variants (/give?status=success etc.) land on /pricing through the same rule.
# That is intended: no receipt compatibility is required, and there is no
# donor history to acknowledge.
#
# Spanish uses ?lang=es because this branch is cut from the deployed main,
# which has no /es/precios route. The localized sales routes ship with the
# coordinated release.
/give                      /pricing           301
/es/dar                    /pricing?lang=es   301
/give-terms                /pricing           301
/es/terminos-de-donacion   /pricing?lang=es   301
